{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-110535","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177904","text":"The companion carries what is waiting on you — 2026-09-11"}]},{"id":"blk-110536","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177905","text":"The mobile companion could see seven projection collections and none of them was the one a companion exists for. Every screen was built from "},{"id":"spn-177906","marks":["code"],"text":"development_tasks"},{"id":"spn-177907","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-177908","marks":["code"],"text":"development_attempts"},{"id":"spn-177909","text":", so \"Needs me\" meant "},{"id":"spn-177910","marks":["italic"],"text":"a plan needs review"},{"id":"spn-177911","text":". Meanwhile the operator projection has carried, since long before the phone existed:"}]},{"id":"blk-110537","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"\"grant_requests\"    => Enum.filter(GrantRegistry.requests(),  &(&1[\"status\"] == \"pending\"))\n\"pending_approvals\" => Enum.filter(Approvals.all(),           &(&1[\"status\"] == \"pending\"))"},{"id":"blk-110538","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177912","text":"Those two are the runtime "},{"id":"spn-177913","marks":["italic"],"text":"stopped"},{"id":"spn-177914","text":", waiting on a person — the desktop's own first two sections are \"Waiting on you · Consent for one effect\". They were the two collections not on the wire."}]},{"id":"blk-110539","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177915","text":"The visible symptom: with nothing to review, the Needs me screen printed "},{"id":"spn-177916","marks":["bold"],"text":"\"Nothing is waiting on a decision.\""},{"id":"spn-177917","text":" It had no basis for that sentence. On Travis's own host, which has zero development tasks, it was the only sentence the screen could produce — while a held effect there would have been invisible."}]},{"id":"blk-110540","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177918","text":"What the phone now receives, and what it does not"}]},{"id":"blk-110541","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177919","text":"Both queues are published, "},{"id":"spn-177920","marks":["bold"],"text":"narrowed to a named set of fields"},{"id":"spn-177921","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-177922","marks":["code"],"text":"cockpit/src/mobile_gateway.rs"},{"id":"spn-177923","text":":"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-110543","spans":[{"id":"spn-177924","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-110544","spans":[{"id":"spn-177925","text":"published"}]}],"id":"blk-110542","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-110545","spans":[{"id":"spn-177926","marks":["code"],"text":"pending_approvals"}]},{"id":"blk-110546","spans":[{"id":"spn-177927","marks":["code"],"text":"id · status · capability · actor · resource · placement"}]}],[{"id":"blk-110547","spans":[{"id":"spn-177928","marks":["code"],"text":"grant_requests"}]},{"id":"blk-110548","spans":[{"id":"spn-177929","marks":["code"],"text":"id · status · capability · actor · resource · requested_duration · created_at · reason"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-110549","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177930","text":"Every other collection in the snapshot goes out as the runtime wrote it, because a workspace or a lane is an inventory record. These two are not. A pending approval carries "},{"id":"spn-177931","marks":["code"],"text":"envelope"},{"id":"spn-177932","text":" — the arguments of the effect nobody has consented to yet — and "},{"id":"spn-177933","marks":["code"],"text":"held_ctx"},{"id":"spn-177934","text":", the caller's whole context; a grant request merges its caller's fields into the stored record wholesale. So this is the one place in the gateway where the allowlist is over "},{"id":"spn-177935","marks":["bold"],"text":"fields"},{"id":"spn-177936","text":" rather than collections, and a field the runtime adds later does not reach a phone until someone names it."}]},{"id":"blk-110550","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177937","marks":["code"],"text":"cargo test mobile_gateway"},{"id":"spn-177938","text":" puts a credential in "},{"id":"spn-177939","marks":["code"],"text":"held_ctx"},{"id":"spn-177940","text":" and a command line in "},{"id":"spn-177941","marks":["code"],"text":"envelope"},{"id":"spn-177942","text":" and asserts neither appears anywhere in the serialised snapshot."}]},{"id":"blk-110551","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177943","marks":["bold"],"text":"The phone still cannot answer."},{"id":"spn-177944","text":" The gateway answers 405 to everything but snapshot, pair and logout, and the cards say so: "},{"id":"spn-177945","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"answered in desktop Super, not here.\""},{"id":"spn-177946","text":" Whether a phone may ever consent is an authority question — gateway, connector, cockpit and ampd — and is not opened here. Telling a person they are being asked is worth doing on its own."}]},{"id":"blk-110552","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177947","text":"The distinction the screen is built on"}]},{"id":"blk-110553","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177948","text":"An empty list means "},{"id":"spn-177949","marks":["bold"],"text":"nobody is asking you"},{"id":"spn-177950","text":". A withheld list means "},{"id":"spn-177951","marks":["bold"],"text":"this app does not know"},{"id":"spn-177952","text":". They are one character apart in JSON and opposite in meaning, and a screen about being asked that prints the first when it means the second has told the person the one thing they cannot check from the phone."}]},{"id":"blk-110554","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177953","text":"So:"}]},{"id":"blk-110555","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110557","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177954","text":"a collection that is not a list is published as "},{"id":"spn-177955","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-177956","text":", never as "},{"id":"spn-177957","marks":["code"],"text":"[]"},{"id":"spn-177958","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-110556","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110559","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177959","text":"the app reads "},{"id":"spn-177960","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-177961","text":" as unavailable and draws "},{"id":"spn-177962","marks":["code"],"text":"--"},{"id":"spn-177963","text":" for the count, not "},{"id":"spn-177964","marks":["code"],"text":"00"},{"id":"spn-177965","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-110558","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110561","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177966","text":"the unavailable case gets its own card naming which queue was not published;"}]}],"id":"blk-110560","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110563","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177967","text":"a single unreadable record is counted and reported, not fatal — one bad row"}]}],"id":"blk-110562","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110564","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177968","text":"must not cost the person the rest of the queue."}]},{"id":"blk-110565","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177969","text":"A record without a "},{"id":"spn-177970","marks":["code"],"text":"capability"},{"id":"spn-177971","text":" is counted as unreadable rather than drawn: a card saying somebody wants something without saying what sends the person to the desktop to find out what they were told. An "},{"id":"spn-177972","marks":["italic"],"text":"empty"},{"id":"spn-177973","text":" "},{"id":"spn-177974","marks":["code"],"text":"actor"},{"id":"spn-177975","text":" is a real value in this runtime and draws as \"No actor is named\"."}]},{"id":"blk-110566","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-177976","text":"Evidence"}]},{"id":"blk-110567","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110569","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177977","marks":["code"],"text":"cargo test mobile_gateway"},{"id":"spn-177978","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-177979","marks":["bold"],"text":"6 passed, 0 failed"},{"id":"spn-177980","text":" (4 new: the field"}]}],"id":"blk-110568","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110570","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177981","text":"allowlist, the grant-request narrowing, a non-list withheld rather than emptied, an empty list not confused with a withheld one)."}]},{"id":"blk-110571","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110573","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177982","marks":["code"],"text":"node --test mobile/test/gateway.test.mjs"},{"id":"spn-177983","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-177984","marks":["bold"],"text":"11 passed, 0 failed"},{"id":"spn-177985","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-110572","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110575","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177986","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/gates.sh"},{"id":"spn-177987","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-177988","marks":["bold"],"text":"8 held · 0 failed · 0 could not run"},{"id":"spn-177989","text":"; webview ACL 35 held"}]}],"id":"blk-110574","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110576","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177990","text":"(no command changed), intent surface 6 held covering 25/25 mutations."}]},{"id":"blk-110577","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110579","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177991","marks":["code"],"text":"cargo build --release --offline"},{"id":"spn-177992","text":" — clean. **The running desktop was not"}]}],"id":"blk-110578","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110580","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177993","text":"restarted**: a restart revokes every paired session, and Travis's phone has held one since 16:19. The new binary is on disk for the next launch."}]},{"id":"blk-110581","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110583","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-177994","text":"App side, "},{"id":"spn-177995","marks":["code"],"text":"work/super-native"},{"id":"spn-177996","text":": "},{"id":"spn-177997","marks":["code"],"text":"npx tsc --noEmit"},{"id":"spn-177998","text":" clean, "},{"id":"spn-177999","marks":["code"],"text":"npm test"},{"id":"spn-178000","text":" **39"}]}],"id":"blk-110582","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110584","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178001","text":"passed, 0 failed** (6 new)."}]},{"id":"blk-110585","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110587","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178002","text":"Rendered on the Android emulator against "},{"id":"spn-178003","marks":["code"],"text":"work/fixture-host.mjs"},{"id":"spn-178004","text":", which runs"}]}],"id":"blk-110586","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110588","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178005","text":"Super's real connector in front of its real gateway:"}]},{"id":"blk-110589","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110591","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178006","text":"populated — "},{"id":"spn-178007","marks":["bold"],"text":"02 waiting on you"},{"id":"spn-178008","text":", a HELD ON CONSENT card"}]}],"id":"blk-110590","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110592","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178009","text":"("},{"id":"spn-178010","marks":["code"],"text":"github.repo.write"},{"id":"spn-178011","text":", asked by kestrel, over traaviis/trvm, placement local) and a GRANT REQUESTED card ("},{"id":"spn-178012","marks":["code"],"text":"fs.read"},{"id":"spn-178013","text":", for the workspace, with its reason and its age), above the plan cards, with \"1 request the host published could not be read on this phone\" beneath them;"}]},{"id":"blk-110593","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110595","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178014","marks":["code"],"text":"--damaged"},{"id":"spn-178015","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-178016","marks":["bold"],"text":"`--` waiting on you"},{"id":"spn-178017","text":", the readable request still drawn, and"}]}],"id":"blk-110594","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110596","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178018","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"This app cannot see what is waiting on you.\""},{"id":"spn-178019","text":" naming held effects as the queue that was not published."}]},{"id":"blk-110597","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-178020","text":"Not done here"}]},{"id":"blk-110598","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110600","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178021","marks":["bold"],"text":"No push."},{"id":"spn-178022","text":" The app polls every 5 s while it is frontmost and nothing at all"}]}],"id":"blk-110599","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110601","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178023","text":"while it is backgrounded, so a held effect arriving while the phone is in a pocket is not noticed until the person opens the app. Every comparable product notifies on an approval gate. That needs a push transport and is a separate decision — a private tailnet has no relay to push through."}]},{"id":"blk-110602","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110604","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178024","marks":["bold"],"text":"No \"how long has this been held\"."},{"id":"spn-178025","text":" "},{"id":"spn-178026","marks":["code"],"text":"Approvals.new_pending/1"},{"id":"spn-178027","text":" writes no"}]}],"id":"blk-110603","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-110605","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178028","text":"timestamp, so the phone has none and invents none. Grant requests carry "},{"id":"spn-178029","marks":["code"],"text":"created_at"},{"id":"spn-178030","text":" and it is shown."}]},{"id":"blk-110606","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-110608","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-178031","marks":["bold"],"text":"No answer path."},{"id":"spn-178032","text":" See above; it is an authority question, not a UI one."}]}],"id":"blk-110607","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieracue2sn6tzho7fimkq7qyq563br4wwzqhzixnwlqnyvnxavyytfva","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}